Subject: [PATCH 11289/11362] Diagnose the exp7025/7026 cascade: a provenance
 rule narrower than its concept

The cascade line fired and GATE_BLOCK moved 10 to 13. The +3 is exactly three
exp7026 retries, so the movement is fully explained by this one chain and is not a
broader regression.

exp7025 passed 22 of 23 preconditions and failed only live_trace_execution, on
"model_filename must be one GGUF filename". The producer takes the basename of the
path the server reports; llama.cpp resolves symlinks, so in a HuggingFace cache
that basename is a content-addressed blob id with no extension. The validator
requires a bare name ending .gguf.

Verified by readlink that the blob is the target of a real
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf in snapshots/, so the readable name exists one link
away. model_hash already carries exactness as a labeled SHA-256 validated in the
same function, so the blob id identifies the model more precisely than a filename
while failing a check that enforces shape and calls it identity.

Not acted on: the file belongs to the live milestone's own task chain, and editing
a file a live chain owns is the collision that cost work three times today. Both
candidate repairs are recorded for its owner.

